cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite the talk it was
  written for, using the metadata in preferred-citation.
type: software
title: "Neighborhood DNA: functional profiles of urban neighbourhoods from Overture Maps Places"
abstract: >-
  A 50-line Python script that turns a bounding box into the functional
  profile of every H3 cell inside it. DuckDB reads the Overture Maps Places
  GeoParquet on S3 and pushes the bounding-box filter down to storage, so
  nothing is downloaded. Each cell gets its shares of taxonomy categories
  (the DNA), Hill numbers of order 1 and 2, the top category share, a TF-IDF
  signature and an HDBSCAN label, written as GeoJSON. The repository adds the
  robustness checks presented at FOSS4G Hiroshima 2026: control for cell size
  and control for the provider blend recorded in the sources column.
